@gotthardp we discussed this in our weekly OTC meeting, and the end result was that we need more details to understand if this use case is supposed to be supported.

It would actually be very helpful if you could design a minimal working example (potentially to be incorporated in our tests if indeed we should support this use case for 3.0).

Would you be able to help us investigate this issue?

@t8m the `try_key_value()` seems to work, but it requires the user to load the default provider explicitly. In my view the user should not need to investigate what providers are needed to perform an operation-- the "dependent" providers (e.g. the default provider for decoding pubkeys) should(?) be loaded by the main provider, but the `try_key_value()` uses the "app-level" libctx, where I cannot "inject" any extra decoders that haven't been loaded by the user. (Or?)
BTW, before 29bf83c889c44236f33004ea2a6126c6d92e8b7a the decoding used to work even without loading the default provider explicitly. But I understand I misused some legacy path.

@mattcaswell yes, I have an (almost) full key manager and a store that calls a foreign decoder. The trouble is the key is not exported by the decoder, but passed directly as a reference, because the system thinks the decoder is from the same provider as the key management. (But it isn't.)
